{% comment %}
  zs-shortlinks.liquid — QR / short-link redirects.

  The QR codes printed on packaging point at simple paths like
  zerostickgaming.com/DSE_Box. Those paths don't exist as real pages, so
  Shopify serves the 404 template — and theme.liquid renders this snippet
  on every 404. When the path matches one of our short links, the browser
  is sent to the destination immediately: the <meta refresh> works even
  with JavaScript turned off, and the script makes it instant and keeps
  the dead 404 page out of the phone's back button.

  To add a new short link later: copy the two-line "when / assign" pair
  below, put the new path in lowercase (both with and without a trailing
  slash), and set the destination URL. Case doesn't matter to visitors —
  the path is lowercased before matching.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign zs_path = request.path | downcase -%}
{%- assign zs_go = nil -%}

{%- case zs_path -%}
  {%- when '/dse_box_label', '/dse_box_label/', '/dse_box', '/dse_box/' -%}
    {%- comment -%} The two DSE packaging QR codes -> the DSE video {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign zs_go = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gRXz2YZY388' -%}
{%- endcase -%}

{%- if zs_go -%}
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ zs_go }}">
  <script>window.location.replace({{ zs_go | json }});</script>
{%- endif -%}
